        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'Hit by both sides': US war on Iran threatens Iraq's 'careful strategy of multi-alignment' Middle East Issued on: 06/04/2026 - 09:15 Catherine Viette is pleased to welcome Dr Renad Mansour, Deputy Director for the Middle East and North Africa Programme and Director of the Iraq Initiative at Chatham House. For years, Iraq has pursued a strategy of multi-alignment, explains Dr. Mansour, carefully maintaining relations with both Iran and the United States to avoid being drawn into regional conflict. However, Iraq’s capacity to remain neutral is diminishing, as the US-Israeli war on Iran threatens political and economic stability across the Middle East. War in the Middle East: Israeli strike on South Beirut kills at least 4 people 05/04/2026 Middle East War in the Middle East: the US rescues missing airman from Iran 05/04/2026 Middle East US war on Iran: Trump pressures allies in war effort but offers 'no role in strategy' 05/04/2026 Middle East French boats set sail from Marseille to join Gaza aid Flotilla 05/04/2026 Middle East \"We got him!\": US rescues aviator whose fighter jet was shot down in Iran 05/04/2026 Middle East US aviator missing after Iran shot down fighter jet has been rescued 05/04/2026 Middle East Lebanon: In the city of Tyre, Christians mark Easter in a ghost town 05/04/2026 Middle East Ramstein: Controversy in Germany over military base's role in Middle East war 05/04/2026 Middle East Sri Lanka struggles to avert economic collapse over Mideast war 05/04/2026 Middle East"
